.Dd 2026-10-15 20:00:00
.Dt TRANSACTIONS 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm transactions
.Nd konsep transaction, ACID, dan serializability
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Ini catatan Chapter 14 dari buku Database System Concepts. Isinya:
konsep transaction, state, concurrent execution, serializability,
recoverability, implementation of isolation, transaction definition
in SQL, dan testing for serializability.
.Pp
Bahasa santai. Tiap konsep dijelasin kenapa dia ada. Karena
transaction itu fondasi database yang bener. Kalau kamu nggak
paham transaction, kamu nggak paham kenapa database bisa
diandelin buat duit.
.Ss Bagian 1: Kenapa Perlu Transaction?
.Sy Contoh klasik:
Transfer $50 dari rekening A ke rekening B.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
1. read(A)
2. A := A - 50
3. write(A)
4. read(B)
5. B := B + 50
6. write(B)
.Ed
.Sy Masalah:
Kalau sistem crash setelah step 3 tapi sebelum step 6, uangnya
"hilang". A udah dikurangi 50, tapi B belum ditambah 50.
.Pp
.Sy Solusi:
Transaction. Kumpulan operasi yang harus jalan sebagai satu
kesatuan.
.Ss Bagian 2: ACID Properties
Empat properti yang harus dipenuhi transaction:
.Bl -tag -width "Durability" -offset indent
.It Sy Atomicity
Entah semua operasi ke-reflect di database, atau nggak sama
sekali. Kalau gagal di tengah, harus di-rollback.
.It Sy Consistency
Eksekusi transaction in isolation preserve konsistensi database.
Contoh: sum(A+B) nggak berubah.
.It Sy Isolation
Walau multiple transaction jalan concurrently, tiap transaction
harus unaware sama transaction lain. Intermediate result harus
hidden.
.It Sy Durability
Setelah transaction commit, perubahannya persist, walau ada
system failure.
.El
.Ss Bagian 2.1: Atomicity dan Durability
.Sy Atomicity:
Kalau transaction gagal setelah step 3 tapi sebelum step 6,
sistem harus mastiin update partial nggak ke-reflect.
.Pp
.Sy Durability:
Setelah user dikasih tau transaction selesai, update harus
persist walau software atau hardware failure.
.Ss Bagian 2.2: Consistency
.Sy Contoh:
Sum A dan B nggak berubah oleh eksekusi transaction.
.Pp
.Sy Consistency requirement:
.Bl -bullet -offset indent
.It
Explicit integrity constraint: primary key, foreign key.
.It
Implicit integrity constraint: sum of balances = cash-in-hand.
.El
.Sy Aturan:
.Bl -bullet -offset indent
.It
Transaction, saat mulai, must see consistent database.
.It
Selama eksekusi, database boleh temporarily inconsistent.
.It
Saat transaction complete, database must be consistent.
.El
.Sy Erroneous transaction logic
bisa bikin inconsistency. Transaction management nggak bisa
detect ini.
.Ss Bagian 2.3: Isolation
.Sy Masalah:
Kalau antara step 3 dan 6, transaction T2 access database yang
partially updated, dia bakal lihat sum A+B yang salah.
.Pp
.Sy Contoh:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
T1                T2
read(A)
A := A - 50
write(A)
                  read(A), read(B), print(A+B)
read(B)
B := B + 50
write(B)
.Ed
.Sy T2
lihat state inconsistent.
.Pp
.Sy Solusi:
Isolation. Transaction jalan serially (satu per satu). Tapi
ini bikin concurrency rendah.
.Ss Bagian 3: Transaction State
Transaction punya 5 state:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
              +------------------+
              |                  |
              v                  |
    +---------+--------+         |
    |      active      |         |
    +---------+--------+         |
              |                  |
              v                  |
    +---------+--------+         |
    | partially        |         |
    | committed        |         |
    +---------+--------+         |
              |                  |
              v                  |
    +---------+--------+         |
    |    committed     |         |
    +------------------+         |
                                 |
    +------------------+         |
    |      failed      |---------+
    +---------+--------+
              |
              v
    +------------------+
    |     aborted      |
    +------------------+
.Ed
.Bl -tag -width "Partially committed" -offset indent
.It Sy Active
State awal. Transaction executing.
.It Sy Partially committed
Setelah final statement executed.
.It Sy Failed
Setelah ketemu bahwa normal execution nggak bisa lanjut.
.It Sy Aborted
Setelah transaction di-rollback dan database di-restore ke
state sebelumnya. Dua opsi:
.Bl -bullet -offset indent
.It
Restart transaction (kalau nggak ada logical error).
.It
Kill transaction.
.El
.It Sy Committed
Setelah successful completion.
.El
.Ss Bagian 4: Concurrent Executions
.Sy Kenapa perlu concurrent?
.Bl -tag -width "Better throughput" -offset indent
.It Sy Increased throughput
Satu transaction pakai CPU sementara yang lain baca/tulis disk.
.It Sy Reduced response time
Short transaction nggak perlu nunggu long transaction.
.El
.Sy Concurrency control schemes:
Mekanisme buat achieve isolation. Ngatur interaksi antar
concurrent transaction.
.Ss Bagian 5: Schedule
.Sy Schedule
= sequence of instruction yang specify chronological order di
mana instruction of concurrent transaction dieksekusi.
.Pp
.Sy Syarat:
.Bl -bullet -offset indent
.It
Harus consist of all instruction of those transactions.
.It
Harus preserve order di mana instruction muncul di tiap
transaction.
.El
.Sy Transaction yang sukses:
Punya commit instruction sebagai last statement.
.Sy Transaction yang gagal:
Punya abort instruction sebagai last statement.
.Ss Bagian 5.1: Serial Schedule
.Sy Contoh:
T1 transfer $50 dari A ke B.
T2 transfer 10% balance dari A ke B.
.Pp
.Sy Serial schedule (T1 dulu, baru T2):
.Bd -literal -offset indent
T1                  T2
read(A)
A := A - 50
write(A)
read(B)
B := B + 50
write(B)
commit
                    read(A)
                    temp := A * 0.1
                    A := A - temp
                    write(A)
                    read(B)
                    B := B + temp
                    write(B)
                    commit
.Ed
.Sy Serial schedule (T2 dulu, baru T1):
Sama, tapi order-nya kebalik.
.Ss Bagian 5.2: Concurrent Schedule
.Sy Schedule yang equivalent dengan serial:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
T1                  T2
read(A)
A := A - 50
write(A)
                    read(A)
                    temp := A * 0.1
                    A := A - temp
                    write(A)
read(B)
B := B + 50
write(B)
commit
                    read(B)
                    B := B + temp
                    write(B)
                    commit
.Ed
.Sy Schedule yang TIDAK preserve sum A+B:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
T1                  T2
read(A)
A := A - 50
                    read(A)
                    temp := A * 0.1
                    A := A - temp
                    write(A)
                    read(B)
write(A)
read(B)
B := B + 50
write(B)
commit
                    B := B + temp
                    write(B)
                    commit
.Ed
.Ss Bagian 6: Serializability
.Sy Basic assumption:
Tiap transaction preserve database consistency.
.Pp
.Sy Serial execution
of set of transaction preserve database consistency.
.Pp
.Sy Schedule
(possibly concurrent) serializable kalau equivalent dengan
serial schedule.
.Pp
.Sy Dua bentuk equivalence:
.Bl -enun -offset indent
.It
Conflict serializability.
.It
View serializability.
.El
.Ss Bagian 6.1: Conflict Serializability
.Sy Kita ignore operations selain read dan write.
.Pp
.Sy Conflict:
Dua instruction
.Sy l_i
dan
.Sy l_j
dari transaction
.Sy T_i
dan
.Sy T_j
conflict kalau ada item Q yang diakses oleh keduanya, dan
minimal satu write Q.
.Bl -enun -offset indent
.It
.Sy read(Q), read(Q) :
nggak conflict.
.It
.Sy read(Q), write(Q) :
conflict.
.It
.Sy write(Q), read(Q) :
conflict.
.It
.Sy write(Q), write(Q) :
conflict.
.El
.Sy Intuisi:
Conflict antara
.Sy l_i
dan
.Sy l_j
forces logical temporal order.
.Ss Bagian 6.2: Conflict Equivalent
.Sy Schedule S
bisa ditransform jadi
.Sy S'
dengan series of swaps of non-conflicting instruction, maka
S dan S' conflict equivalent.
.Sy Schedule S
conflict serializable kalau conflict equivalent ke serial
schedule.
.Ss Bagian 6.3: Precedence Graph
.Sy Definisi:
Directed graph dengan vertex = transaction.
.Pp
.Sy Arc
dari
.Sy T_i
ke
.Sy T_j
kalau dua transaction conflict, dan
.Sy T_i
accessed data item yang conflict duluan.
.Pp
.Sy Theorem:
Schedule conflict serializable jika dan hanya jika precedence
graph-nya acyclic.
.Pp
.Sy Cycle detection:
O(n^2) atau O(n+e).
.Pp
.Sy Kalau acyclic:
Serializability order didapat dari topological sorting.
.Ss Bagian 6.4: View Serializability
.Sy Definisi:
Dua schedule S dan S' view equivalent kalau:
.Bl -enun -offset indent
.It
Kalau di S, T_i reads initial value of Q, maka di S' juga.
.It
Kalau di S, T_i reads value yang diproduksi T_j, maka di S'
juga.
.It
Transaction yang performs final write(Q) di S harus juga di S'.
.El
.Sy Schedule S
view serializable kalau view equivalent ke serial schedule.
.Pp
.Sy Setiap conflict serializable
juga view serializable.
.Sy Tapi nggak sebaliknya.
.Pp
.Sy Contoh view serializable tapi bukan conflict serializable:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
T27      T28      T29
read(Q)
         write(Q)
                  write(Q)
write(Q)
.Ed
.Sy Ini punya blind writes.
.Pp
.Sy Testing view serializability:
NP-complete. Nggak ada efficient algorithm.
.Ss Bagian 7: Recoverability
.Ss Bagian 7.1: Recoverable Schedule
.Sy Definisi:
Kalau T_j reads data item yang sebelumnya ditulis T_i, maka
commit operation T_i harus muncul sebelum commit operation T_j.
.Pp
.Sy Contoh yang NOT recoverable:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
T8            T9
read(A)
write(A)
              read(A)
              commit
read(B)
.Ed
.Sy Kalau T8 abort:
T9 udah baca (dan mungkin nunjukin ke user) state inconsistent.
.Ss Bagian 7.2: Cascading Rollback
.Sy Definisi:
Single transaction failure leads to series of transaction
rollback.
.Pp
.Sy Contoh:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
T10            T11            T12
read(A)
               read(B)
write(A)
               abort
                              read(A)
                              read(A)
.Ed
.Sy Kalau T10 fails:
T11 dan T12 harus di-rollback. Ini yang disebut cascading
rollback.
.Ss Bagian 7.3: Cascadeless Schedule
.Sy Definisi:
Buat tiap pair T_i dan T_j di mana T_j reads data item yang
sebelumnya ditulis T_i, commit operation T_i muncul sebelum
read operation T_j.
.Pp
.Sy Setiap cascadeless
juga recoverable.
.Sy Tapi nggak sebaliknya.
.Ss Bagian 8: Concurrency Control
.Sy Database harus provide mechanism
yang mastiin semua schedule:
.Bl -bullet -offset indent
.It
Conflict serializable.
.It
Recoverable, preferably cascadeless.
.El
.Sy Policy "one transaction at a time":
Generate serial schedule, tapi poor concurrency.
.Pp
.Sy Concurrency-control schemes:
Trade-off antara amount of concurrency dan overhead.
.Pp
.Sy Testing schedule after execution:
Terlalu telat. Tests for serializability bantu kita ngerti
kenapa protocol bener.
.Ss Bagian 9: Weak Levels of Consistency
.Sy Beberapa aplikasi
willing buat weak consistency, allow schedule yang nggak
serializable.
.Bl -bullet -offset indent
.It
Read-only transaction yang mau approximate total balance.
.It
Database statistics buat query optimization.
.El
.Sy Trade-off:
Accuracy vs performance.
.Ss Bagian 9.1: Level of Consistency SQL-92
.Bl -tag -width "Read uncommitted" -offset indent
.It Sy Serializable
Default. Full isolation.
.It Sy Repeatable read
Cuma committed records yang dibaca. Repeated reads sama.
Tapi mungkin nggak serializable.
.It Sy Read committed
Cuma committed records, tapi successive reads bisa beda.
.It Sy Read uncommitted
Bahkan uncommitted records bisa dibaca.
.El
.Sy Warning:
Beberapa database nggak ensure serializable by default.
Oracle dan PostgreSQL by default support "snapshot isolation".
.Ss Bagian 10: Transaction Definition di SQL
.Sy Transaction begin implicitly.
.Pp
.Sy Transaction ends by:
.Bl -tag -width "COMMIT WORK" -offset indent
.It Sy COMMIT WORK
Commit current transaction, begin new one.
.It Sy ROLLBACK WORK
Cause current transaction to abort.
.El
.Sy Default di hampir semua database:
Setiap SQL statement commits implicitly kalau execute
successfully.
.Sy Implicit commit bisa di-turn off:
Contoh di JDBC:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
connection.setAutoCommit(false);
.Ed
.Ss Ringkasan
.Bd -literal -offset indent
Konsep              Inti
Transaction         Unit of program execution
ACID                Atomicity, Consistency, Isolation, Durability
Atomicity           All or nothing
Consistency         Preserve consistency
Isolation           Unaware of others
Durability          Persist after commit
Transaction state   active, partially committed, failed,
                    aborted, committed
Schedule            Sequence of instructions
Serial schedule     Transactions one after another
Serializability      Equivalent to serial schedule
Conflict            read/write dari item yang sama
Conflict serializable  Equivalent via swap non-conflict
Precedence graph    Directed graph transaksi
Recoverable         Commit T_i sebelum commit T_j
Cascading rollback  One failure -> multiple rollback
Cascadeless         Commit T_i sebelum read T_j
Weak consistency    Trade-off accuracy
SQL isolation level Serializable, repeatable read,
                    read committed, read uncommitted
SQL transaction     COMMIT WORK, ROLLBACK WORK
.Ed
Kalau kamu cuma inget satu hal dari catatan ini, inget ini:
.Sy transaction itu bukan cuma soal "commit" atau "rollback".
Dia soal jaminan bahwa database tetap konsisten walau ada
failure, concurrent access, atau error. ACID itu janji
database ke kamu. Kalau database nggak bisa jaga janji itu,
jangan pakai buat simpen duit.
.Pp
Yang belum dijawab di sini: gimana caranya implement isolation
tanpa bikin concurrency rendah? Kapan pakai locking, kapan
pakai timestamp? Itu topik Chapter 15: Concurrency Control.
